WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.088
Here's the mapping.

2
00:00:01.088 --> 00:00:05.649
A type that mentions maintenance is
maintenance; one that mentions change,

3
00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:10.064
or the action-required type, is a
change; a production event notification

4
00:00:10.064 --> 00:00:14.700
is an incident; and action-recommended
or information types are advisories.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.166
The time fields are read by their types: a
start or new start time opens the window,

6
00:00:20.166 --> 00:00:25.300
an end time closes it, and an action-required-by
time is Oracle's own deadline.

7
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:31.400
Notice what's different from Azure and
Microsoft 365: Oracle flags action itself.

8
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.722
So every action-required OCI
notice says the provider decided,

9
00:00:35.722 --> 00:00:38.110
and the kit needs no rule of its own.
